# .trivyignore — CVE suppression list for Trivy scans
# Format: one CVE ID per line (e.g., CVE-2024-XXXXX)
# Optional expiry annotation:
#   CVE-2024-XXXXX  # expires: YYYY-MM-DD

# CVE-2026-40355 — krb5 (MIT Kerberos 5): DoS via NULL pointer dereference
# in NegoEx. Not exploitable in this image: we ship a Python LLM ticket
# solver — we do not run a Kerberos server, do not negotiate NegoEx, and
# the krb5 libraries are only present as transitive system deps that are
# never invoked. Trivy classifies as CRITICAL despite CVSS=medium; safe
# to suppress in our deployment model.
CVE-2026-40355  # expires: 2026-11-24

# CVE-2026-78661 — golang.org/x/net/html DoS via crafted HTML input, in
# golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 compiled into the upstream `gh` binary
# (usr/bin/gh) that Dockerfile and sandbox/Dockerfile install from GitHub's
# apt repo. No fixed `gh` release exists yet: as of 2026-11-09 the latest tag
# (v2.103.3) pins x/net v0.60.0 and cli/cli trunk only v0.61.0 (fix: 0.62.0).
# Impact is limited to a crash of a short-lived CLI process talking to
# GitHub's API. Drop this entry once a `gh` release with x/net >= 0.62.0
# ships (the unpinned apt install picks it up on rebuild).
CVE-2026-78661  # expires: 2026-11-23
